# ============================================================================
# Zero to Production — Phase 2 Hackathon
#
# DOC DIRECTORY SPLIT — read this before adding anything:
#   agent/   = INTERNAL working memory. Planning, runbooks, cut lists, pitch
#              notes, troubleshooting. Written for us, under fatigue, at 17:00.
#              IGNORED — judges never see it, and it must not dilute the repo.
#   docs/    = JUDGE-FACING submission documentation. Architecture overview,
#              API reference, setup guide, deployment guide.
#              TRACKED — this is a scored deliverable (Rulebook §7.1, §9.3).
#
# CLAUDE.md is the agent's operating manual — internal, ignored.
# README.md is the front door for judges — tracked, always.
# ============================================================================

# --- Internal agent working memory (never shipped) --------------------------
agent/
CLAUDE.md

# --- Secrets & credentials (Rulebook §6.2: committing these costs points) ----
.env
.env.*
*.env
secrets/
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
*.pfx
credentials.json
service-account*.json
*-service-account.json
gcp-key*.json
.htpasswd

# ...but the config SURFACE must be visible to judges:
!.env.example
!.env.sample
!.env.template

